# SONGHA — "Tomorrow Can Wait"
# Member file. Rooftop, city lights, star maps, clocks, calendar fragments.
# Record 03. Seed: var.hour (morning / night). Local flag: songha_asked.

=== songha_intro
@show songha thinking at=c
> Songha has claimed the front desk.
> Notebook open. Pen uncapped. His watch unbuckled and laid flat beside the page, so he can read the second hand without turning his wrist.
> It is the most organised anyone has ever looked behind that desk. Including you, the winter it was yours.
songha: Don't read over my shoulder. It's not finished.
songha[smile]: …Okay, read over my shoulder. Tell me if it's stupid.
> The page is headed TONIGHT, underlined twice.
> 00:50 — establish what ECHO is. 01:05 — rooms (consent first). 01:30 — food (Hamin's orders). 03:00 — ???. 04:45 — everyone near the door.
@show daniel laugh at=r
daniel: He's scheduled the haunted building. He does this. He scheduled my birthday.
songha[neutral]: And your birthday ran on time.
daniel: It ran *exactly* on time. People were scared to arrive late. Someone apologised for being early.
songha: Everyone came. That's the point of a party.
@hide daniel
> Daniel wanders off to press something he shouldn't. Without looking up, Songha adds a line: *00:47 — Daniel, buttons. Monitor.*
* [curious] "What's at three o'clock? The question marks."
    @rel songha trust+1
    songha: That's the part I haven't solved yet. There's always a part like that.
    songha: Usually it's the part that ruins the rest.
* [playful] "You've written a schedule for a night with no schedule."
    @rel songha closeness+1
    songha[laugh]: That's *why* it needs one. Nobody else was going to do it.
    songha: Watch. By two a.m. every single one of them will be asking me what time it is.
* [quiet] Read the page properly. Every line.
    @rel songha closeness+1
    > He notices you reading every line. He turns the notebook a quarter-inch so it faces you better.
@if flag.told_worked_here
    songha: You worked this desk, you said. So you're my best source.
    songha: The fuse box. Where is it?
    you: Behind Lost and Found. Under a poster of a cat.
    songha[surprised]: …That's the most useful sentence anyone's said tonight.
    > He writes it down. *Fuse box: cat.*
@show hanbi smile at=r
> Hanbi drifts past the desk and, without being asked, sets a phone charger down beside the watch.
songha: Hyung. How did you know?
hanbi: …Twelve percent. I could see it from the sofa.
@hide hanbi
songha[smile]: He's the only one who ever brings a charger. I've never once had to plan for it. It's unsettling.
songha[thinking]: Anyway. I think I sent something to this archive. When I was seventeen.
songha: A plan. Five years, one page. Which means it's due. {p} This year.
you: Are you on schedule?
songha: Four out of five.
songha: Don't ask about the fifth.
songha: Last thing. I'm doing a rota. Who stays awake, who naps on the sofa if this runs long.
songha: Morning person or night person?
* [sincere] "Morning. I like the part where the day hasn't done anything wrong yet."
    @var hour = "morning"
    @rel songha trust+1
    songha[smile]: That's a good answer. Annoyingly good. Morning. You're on the last shift, then.
* [quiet] "Night. It's quiet. Nobody expects anything from you at night."
    @var hour = "night"
    @rel songha trust+1
    songha: …Yeah. That's fair. Night. You're with me, then. I always end up on the night shift.
* [playful] "I'm a person who is awake right now. Draw your own conclusions."
    @var hour = "night"
    @rel songha closeness+1
    songha[laugh]: That's night. I'm writing night. You don't get to be mysterious on my rota.
> He writes {{playerName}} at the bottom of the list. Then he frowns, draws a neat arrow, and moves it up into the middle, as if the bottom were rude.
* [playful] "You wrote my name very neatly."
    @rel songha closeness+1 romance+1
    songha: I write everything neatly.
    songha[shy]: …Yours got a little extra. It's a long night. Don't tell Daniel.
* [sincere] "Thanks for putting me on it."
    @rel songha trust+1
    songha: You're here. So you're on it. That's how a rota works.
@hub act1

