songha: Don't say anything about the dates.
* [playful] "You dated the check marks."
    @rel songha closeness+1
    songha: I said don't say anything about the dates.
    songha: Year Three took nineteen months. I wanted it on the record.
* [sincere] "That's five years of keeping promises to a seventeen-year-old."
    @rel songha trust+1
    songha: He was very demanding.
    songha[smile]: He was also mostly right. Don't tell him.
* [curious] "Year Five. Why didn't you just look them up?"
    @rel songha trust+1
    songha: Ah. {p} You went straight for it.
songha: The star names. I could have looked them up. It's a thirty-second search.
songha: I've opened the search bar. More than once.
songha: It says *ask*. I don't skip steps.
> It's shaped like a joke. He doesn't laugh at it.
songha: Year One says 5:40. I haven't missed it in five years. Not sick. Not on my birthday.
songha: I'm good at tomorrow. I'm *very* good at tomorrow. I have tomorrow down to the minute.
songha[sad]: It's today I keep skipping.
> His eyes go to his wrist. He does it so often it's almost punctuation.
@textbox echo
echo: Supplementary data. On the night of this record, the owner remained on the roof for sixty-one minutes after the unresolved subject arrived.
echo: Watch checks: zero. This is the lowest figure in the owner's file. I thought it might be of interest.
@textbox normal
songha[laugh]: Thank you, ECHO. Very helpful. Extremely— {p} yeah.
songha: Sixty-one minutes. I don't know how to do that anymore.
* [sincere] "You don't need to know how. You did it once without trying."
    @rel songha trust+1
    songha: Without trying. {p} That's the one part I can't schedule.
* [playful] "I could confiscate it. You'd get it back at five."
    @rel songha closeness+1
    > He actually considers it. You can watch him run the numbers.
    songha: …Ask me again later. I'm not strong enough yet.
