    songha: …Yeah.
    > You don't take the watch off. You only turn his wrist over, gently, so the face points down at the roof instead of up at him.
    > His pulse is right there under the strap. Very steady, for someone who looks this caught out.
    songha[shy]: That's cheating. It's still running.
    you: It can run. You don't have to watch it.
songha: Can I ask you something? It's not planned. I don't have it written down anywhere.
songha: "I always set one for leaving." What did that mean?
* [sincere] "We moved a lot. Leaving on time made it hurt less."
    @rel songha trust+1 closeness+1
    you: I got very good at knowing when to go. The alarm meant I didn't have to decide.
    > He doesn't answer straight away. He doesn't reach for a plan, either. He just lets it sit there, which from him is a lot.
* [playful] "I was an extremely punctual sixteen-year-old. You'd have liked me."
    @rel songha closeness+1
    songha: I did like you. You named a plane Minor Delay.
    songha: That's not an answer, though. Try again. I'll wait. I'm practising.
    you: We moved a lot. Spring was usually when we went. The alarm made leaving a time instead of a decision.
* [quiet] "Spring was always when we left."
    @rel songha trust+1
    > You don't add anything. He doesn't ask you to.
songha: Okay. {p} Here's what I'm going to do.
songha: I'm not going to say something wise. I'm bad at wise. Hanbi-hyung does wise.
songha: I'm just going to point out that tonight, you came *back*. That's on the record. ECHO timestamps everything.
@textbox echo
echo: Confirmed. Recipient {{playerName}} returned to Studio 25 at 00:21.
@textbox normal
songha[smile]: See? Logged. You can't argue with a timestamp.
> Above you, the reconstructed sky turns a few degrees, the way it did five years ago whether anyone was watching or not.
songha: The room's going to close soon. The edges are going soft.
songha[thinking]: And I don't want to plan the next part. {p} That's new. Give me a second with it.
* [romantic] Sit down beside him on the crate. There's just about room. {if songha.closeness >= 2 or songha.trust >= 2}
    @rel songha romance+1
    > There is not just about room. You fit anyway, shoulder to shoulder, the notebook balanced across both your knees.
    songha: This crate was built for one seventeen-year-old.
    you: We're making it work.
    songha[smile]: We are, actually. Structurally unsound and making it work.
* [romantic] "It's Year Five. Ask me." {if songha.trust >= 2}
    @rel songha romance+1 trust+1
    @flag songha_asked
    songha: …Okay.
    songha: What's that one really called?
    > You look up at the orange star. You look at it for a long time.
    you: I have no idea.
    songha[laugh]: You— *five years*—
    you: I left before the app loaded.
    > He laughs so hard he has to cover his mouth again. Some things hold across five years. That laugh. The instinct to hide it.
* [careful] "Take your second. I'm not going anywhere."
    @rel songha trust+1
