=== songha_hub
@if flag.room_songha and not flag.songha_postchat
    @show songha smile at=c
    > Songha is back at the front desk, notebook open to TONIGHT.
    > One line is crossed out. Not erased: one clean stroke, so you can still read it underneath. *02:30 — review ECHO findings (alone).*
    songha: I cancelled a step.
    songha: The findings were "it's you". I already had that. Reviewing it alone seemed inefficient.
    songha[thinking]: So now I have twenty-five minutes with nothing in them. It's very uncomfortable. Apparently that's normal.
    @show hyunjun laugh at=r
    hyunjun: Songha-hyung has *free time*? Convenience store! One more stop! Also, who's Gerald? You came out of your room saying "Gerald".
    songha[neutral]: Gerald is a star. I said it once. And the time isn't free. It's reserved.
    hyunjun: Reserved for what?
    songha: Go away, Hyunjun.
    hyunjun[smile]: That's not a no!
    @hide hyunjun
    > He goes, walking backwards, grinning the whole way to the door.
    > Songha's watch is on the other wrist now, face turned in. Checking it would mean looking at his own palm.
    * [romantic] "So. Reserved for what?" {if songha.romance >= 1}
        @rel songha romance+1
        songha: Haven't decided. That's the point of it.
        songha[shy]: It's twenty-five minutes. I'm keeping it open. You can sit in it, if you want. Like a chair.
        > You sit in it. It turns out to be the sofa. He doesn't open the notebook once.
    * [playful] "Want me to schedule it for you?"
        @rel songha closeness+1
        songha: Absolutely not.
        songha: …What would you put, though. Hypothetically.
        you: "02:30 — nothing. 02:40 — more nothing. 02:55 — review nothing."
        songha[laugh]: That's a terrible plan. Write it down for me.
    * [sincere] "You moved the watch."
        @rel songha trust+1
        songha: Inside of the wrist. Now if I check it, it looks like I'm reading my own palm.
        songha[smile]: It takes an extra second. Turns out one second is enough to change my mind. Sometimes.
    @flag songha_postchat
@elif flag.room_songha
    @show songha smile at=c
    @if rooms() >= 6
        songha: We're ahead of schedule. I hate that I know that. I'm trying to not know that.
    @else
        songha: I still have my twenty-five minutes. Haven't spent them. It's harder than it looks.
    songha: A plane went over ten minutes ago. Minor Delay. I didn't check where it was going.
@else
    @show songha thinking at=c
    @if rooms() == 0
        songha: Nobody's gone through a door yet. Somebody has to be first.
        songha: Statistically, it shouldn't be me. I'd over-prepare and then critique the room.
    @else
        songha: You've been in other rooms. What's it like? Be specific. I can take specifics.
        you: Like walking into somebody's memory, if the memory had air in it.
        songha[thinking]: …That's not specific. That's poetry. {p} It's good, though.
    songha: Mine's a piece of paper. Everyone's asked what's on it. I keep saying "a document". Technically true.
    songha[smile]: The door's not going anywhere. I checked. Twice.
@hub act2

=== songha_route
@chapter route
@time 03:50
@var route = "songha"
@bg studio_rooftop t=slow d=2.4
@amb wind
@music quiet
@fx stars n=0.8
@cam reveal
> The door to the roof sticks the way it always did. Shoulder, then hip, then it gives.
> The rain has moved off east. The concrete still holds it in shallow puddles, and every puddle has a piece of sky in it.
> Songha is sitting on the base of the water tank, notebook on his knee, phone torch propped on its end to light the page.
> He doesn't look up. He is writing very fast.
@show songha thinking at=c
songha: Eight encounters. Six years. Four cities. ECHO says no causal link.
songha: But ECHO's an archive. It files things. It doesn't *solve* them.
> The page is a timeline. Eight dots in a row, each labelled in his small upright hand. Arrows between them that don't point at anything.
songha: If I sort them by season, there's a—
songha: No. There isn't.
you: Are you trying to solve the night?
songha: Someone should.
> He says it without looking up. Then the pen stops.
> For a moment the only sound on the roof is the laundromat vent, breathing warm air four storeys down.
you: Maybe we're supposed to live it.
> He looks at the timeline. Then at you. Then, for the first time since you came up the stairs, at the sky.
songha: That's a very inefficient approach.
songha[smile]: Sit down. You're making the ledge look structurally unsound.
> You sit. The concrete is cold through everything. He moves the phone torch so it isn't in your eyes, without comment.
songha: The thing is, if there's no pattern, then it's just chance. Eight times.
songha[thinking]: I don't know what to do with chance. You can't put it on a rota. You can't prepare for it.
you: You can't prepare for it. You can keep showing up.
songha: …That's what you did. Six years, four cities. You just kept showing up.
songha: And we kept noticing. {p} Okay. I heard it downstairs. I'm still getting used to it.
@music songha
songha: I wasn't hiding, for the record. I had a reason to be up here.
@if var.hour == "morning"
    songha: You said morning. On the rota. First thing tonight.
    songha: Sunrise is 06:14. That's after ECHO, after the power, after the crew. So I checked whether this door locks from the outside.
    songha: It doesn't. So the plan was, you'd get the morning. The real one. From up here.
    you: You planned me a sunrise.
    songha[shy]: I planned *access* to a sunrise. The sunrise does its own thing.
@else
    songha: You said night. On the rota. First thing tonight.
    songha: This is the last of it. After four, it's technically morning. I looked it up. There's a definition. I didn't like it.
    songha: I didn't want you to spend the last hour of your night in a lobby.
    you: You scheduled me the night.
    songha[shy]: I scheduled you a *view* of the night. The night does its own thing.
@if flag.cold
    > He shrugs out of the navy jacket, cream sleeves and the small star patch, and holds it out without ceremony.
    songha: You said you were cold at midnight. It's eleven degrees now. Less with the wind. {p} Don't argue with the numbers.
@else
    > He has already unzipped the navy jacket halfway, like he's been waiting for an excuse.
    songha: It's eleven degrees. I'm not saying you're cold. I'm presenting the data.
* [sincere] Take the jacket. "Thank you."
    @rel songha closeness+1
    > It's warm from him and smells faintly of the studio's old detergent. There's a notebook-shaped pocket inside, empty.
    songha: The pocket's for the notebook. You can use it for your hands. It's a multi-purpose pocket.
* [careful] "Only if you won't freeze."
    @rel songha trust+1
    songha: I've got a hoodie under this and a very strong sense of purpose. Take it.
    > You take it. The inside pocket is exactly notebook-sized.
